elow, 8.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.4 to 6.2. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 27 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,996.50 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be low due to market conditions, or budgets might be fixed. Other reasons could include multiple needs or separate purchases.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of the December contracts to see if they fit a pattern. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same need. Look at contract [1] to see what was purchased and if it aligns with the body's stated goals.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["idIbDAkRPTzI8aL3PRS10Q%3D%3D","QRLX1DTHp%2FeHCIsjvJ3rhQ%3D%3D","6E6zbXf7fZ19Zh%2FyRJgM8w%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}